 with Built-in 13dBi Antenna</h3><p data-start=\"781\" data-end=\"1167\">The <strong data-start=\"785\" data-end=\"837\">Cambium Networks ePMP 1000 5GHz Integrated Radio</strong> is a compact and high-performance wireless solution designed for <strong data-start=\"903\" data-end=\"933\">Point-to-Multipoint (PTMP)</strong> and <strong data-start=\"938\" data-end=\"974\">short-range Point-to-Point (PTP)</strong> deployments. With an integrated <strong data-start=\"1007\" data-end=\"1037\">13 dBi directional antenna</strong> and <strong data-start=\"1042\" data-end=\"1079\">real throughput of up to 200 Mbps</strong>, this radio ensures stable, reliable connectivity in both urban and rural environments.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1169\" data-end=\"1465\">Built for scalability and efficiency, the ePMP 1000 supports <strong data-start=\"1230\" data-end=\"1253\">GPS synchronization</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1255\" data-end=\"1273\">TDD technology</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"1279\" data-end=\"1295\">QoS features</strong> for prioritizing voice, video, and data. ISPs and network integrators widely use it for cost-effective broadband delivery and enterprise networking in Bangladesh.</p><p data-start=\"1169\" data-end=\"1465\"><br></p><h3 data-start=\"1472\" data-end=\"1495\"><strong data-start=\"1478\" data-end=\"1495\">Key Features:</strong></h3>\n<ul data-start=\"1496\" data-end=\"1845\"><li data-start=\"1496\" data-end=\"1538\">\n<p data-start=\"1498\" data-end=\"1538\">Operating Frequency: 5.150 – 5.970 GHz</p>\n</li><li data-start=\"1539\" data-end=\"1584\">\n<p data-start=\"1541\" data-end=\"1584\">Built-in 13 dBi directional panel antenna</p>\n</li><li data-start=\"1585\" data-end=\"1615\">\n<p data-start=\"1587\" data-end=\"1615\">Throughput: Up to 200 Mbps</p>\n</li><li data-start=\"1616\" data-end=\"1677\">\n<p data-start=\"1618\" data-end=\"1677\">TDD GPS synchronization (when paired with compatible APs)</p>\n</li><li data-start=\"1678\" data-end=\"1719\">\n<p data-start=\"1680\" data-end=\"1719\">Supports PTMP &amp; short-range PTP modes</p>\n</li><li data-start=\"1720\" data-end=\"1768\">\n<p data-start=\"1722\" data-end=\"1768\">Low latency and interference-tolerant design</p>\n</li><li data-start=\"1769\" data-end=\"1809\">\n<p data-start=\"1771\" data-end=\"1809\">Compact outdoor IP55-rated enclosure</p>\n</li><li data-start=\"1810\" data-end=\"1845\">\n<p data-start=\"1812\" data-end=\"1845\">Ideal for CPE or short PTP link</p></li></ul><h3 data-start=\"1852\" data-end=\"1878\"><strong data-start=\"1858\" data-end=\"1876\">Link Distance:</strong></h3>\n<ul data-start=\"1879\" data-end=\"1997\"><li data-start=\"1879\" data-end=\"1937\">\n<p data-start=\"1881\" data-end=\"1937\"><strong data-start=\"1881\" data-end=\"1896\">PTMP Range:</strong> Up to <strong data-start=\"1903\" data-end=\"1914\">5–10 km</strong> (with GPS-synced AP)</p>\n</li><li data-start=\"1938\" data-end=\"1997\">\n<p data-start=\"1940\" data-end=\"1997\"><strong data-start=\"1940\" data-end=\"1959\">Short PTP Link:</strong> Up to <strong data-start=\"1966\" data-end=\"1975\">15 km</strong> (clear line-of-sight)</p><p data-start=\"1940\" data-end=\"1997\"><br></p></li></ul><h3 data-start=\"2004\" data-end=\"2035\"><strong data-start=\"2010\" data-end=\"2033\">Ideal Applications:</strong></h3>\n<ul data-start=\"2036\" data-end=\"2167\"><li data-start=\"2036\" data-end=\"2077\">\n<p data-start=\"2038\" data-end=\"2077\">ISP customer premises equipment (CPE)</p>\n</li><li data-start=\"2078\" data-end=\"2109\">\n<p data-start=\"2080\" data-end=\"2109\">Short-distance PTP backhaul</p>\n</li><li data-start=\"2110\" data-end=\"2141\">\n<p data-start=\"2112\" data-end=\"2141\">Wireless video surveillance</p>\n</li><li data-start=\"2142\" data-end=\"2167\">\n<p data-start=\"2144\" data-end=\"2167\">Rural internet access</p></li></ul>\n              "},{"title":"Product Table","active":false,"cls":"tab-4","noExpand":false,"kind":"compat","title2":"Product